Drop-in module load checks for ci/boot.sh: each *.txt file lists module
names (one per line, # comments allowed). The boot test runs
`modprobe <mod> && rmmod <mod>` for each and expects the marker
"RLINUX-CI: load <mod> ok". Use one file per driver so parallel PRs don't
conflict. Build the module as =m in a ci/config.d fragment.
